# API Documentation

## Base URL

`https://api.yourproject.com`

## Authentication

All API requests require a valid JWT token in the Authorization header:

```
Authorization: Bearer your_token_here
```

## Endpoints

{% for namespace in namespaces %}
### {{ namespace }}

{% for model in models %}
#### {{ model }}

- `GET /api/{{ namespace|lower }}/{{ model|lower }}s`: List all {{ model|lower }}s
- `POST /api/{{ namespace|lower }}/{{ model|lower }}s`: Create a new {{ model|lower }}
- `GET /api/{{ namespace|lower }}/{{ model|lower }}s/{id}`: Get a specific {{ model|lower }}
- `PUT /api/{{ namespace|lower }}/{{ model|lower }}s/{id}`: Update a specific {{ model|lower }}
- `DELETE /api/{{ namespace|lower }}/{{ model|lower }}s/{id}`: Delete a specific {{ model|lower }}
- `GET /api/{{ namespace|lower }}/{{ model|lower }}s/search/{term}`: Search {{ model|lower }}s
- `POST /api/{{ namespace|lower }}/{{ model|lower }}s/filter`: Filter {{ model|lower }}s

{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}

## Response Format

All responses are in JSON format and include a `data` object and a `message` string:

```json
{
  "data": {},
  "message": "Success message"
}
```

## Error Handling

Errors are returned with appropriate HTTP status codes and include an error message:

```json
{
  "message": "Error message"
}
```

